# Local development environment.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored via the `.env.*` rule, with `!.env.example`
# keeping this file itself tracked) and fill in what you need.
#
# ## The client reads exactly one of these
#
# `VITE_API_BASE` is the repository's only `import.meta.env` read
# (`src/account/session.ts`), and it is asserted as the only one. An empty value
# means same-origin, which is what `npm run dev` and production both want; it
# exists for a preview where the app and the API are on different hosts.
VITE_API_BASE=

# ## Server secrets are not here
#
# The Worker's secrets are set with `wrangler secret put NAME` and never live in
# a file this repository tracks. The one this phase needs is:
#
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID   the OAuth client id a Google ID token's `aud` must equal.
#                      `server/google.ts` checks it, and `/api/config` serves it
#                      to the browser (it is not a secret — it travels in every
#                      OAuth request).
#
# For `wrangler dev` the same names go in `.dev.vars`, which `.gitignore`
# already covers (`.dev.vars*`). It is a different file because a Worker's
# environment is not Vite's: `VITE_`-prefixed variables are inlined into the
# client bundle at build time, and everything else is available to the server at
# runtime. Confusing the two would either leak a secret into the bundle or
# silently give the Worker an undefined variable.
#
# `.dev.vars` example:
#
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
